# Documentation updates

When you add a **new feature** or **change existing behavior**, update the relevant docs so they stay accurate. Do not leave documentation outdated.

## Where to update

- **Feature behavior / UX** — [docs/03-FEATURES.md](docs/03-FEATURES.md): add or edit sections for the feature (e.g. how it works, where it lives in the codebase).
- **Users, roles, access** — [docs/01-USERS_AND_ACCESS.md](docs/01-USERS_AND_ACCESS.md).
- **Auth, login, sessions** — [docs/04-AUTHENTICATION.md](docs/04-AUTHENTICATION.md) (and VERIFICATION_CODE_* if relevant).
- **Scripture / Bible** — [docs/02-BIBLE_AND_SCRIPTURE.md](docs/02-BIBLE_AND_SCRIPTURE.md); [gospel-admin/docs/SCRIPTURE_ACCESS_LOGGING.md](gospel-admin/docs/SCRIPTURE_ACCESS_LOGGING.md) if logging changes.
- **Deployment / infra** — [docs/05-INFRASTRUCTURE.md](docs/05-INFRASTRUCTURE.md), [docs/DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md](docs/DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md).
- **Capacitor / native app** — note in [gospel-admin/README.md](gospel-admin/README.md) or the Capacitor rule if it affects when native apps must be redeployed.
- **Deploy update notice (user-visible releases)** — append the **same** plain-language note to [gospel-admin/data/deploy-update-changelog.json](gospel-admin/data/deploy-update-changelog.json) and [gospel-admin/data/site-changelog.json](gospel-admin/data/site-changelog.json) (see `.cursor/rules/deploy-update-message.mdc`; `npm run append-release-changelog -- "…"` from `gospel-admin/`).
- **Index** — if a new doc is added or a topic moves, update [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) (Core Topics table / Quick Start).

## Practice

- Prefer **editing existing docs** over creating new ones unless the topic is large and separate.
- Keep prose short; link to code or other docs where helpful.
- When changing behavior, remove or rewrite outdated sentences instead of leaving them in place.
